<node id="Platypus AU">
  <data key="d0">Platypus AU</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Platypus AU is an Australian e-commerce storefront representing the Australian branch of the Platypus retail brand. It operates as a distinct GRA storefront specializing in the sale of Platypus branded items within Australia, utilizing the Australian Dollar (AUD) as its currency. The site is implemented using Magento combined with styled-components and employs the PWA Studio stack for its frontend architecture, which includes user interface features such as a flyout menu offering options like "Track My Order," external help links to Zendesk, and pages for delivery information, returns, FAQs, and contact details.

This storefront is integrated with various backend and analytics technologies, including Fredhopper for category management under the code "catalog01_2," Adobe collect endpoints for data capture, and FullStory for session recording to monitor user interactions. The site supports reward programs, particularly enabling customers to earn Qantas Points through purchases. Platypus AU is also involved in multiple testing scenarios: localization testing (notably E2E-LOC-001), concurrency-sensitive race condition testing in the cart overlay, navigation category inventory issue assessments (documented on May 31, 2026), and live reconciliation tests involving key Sydney CBD addresses. 

Operational aspects further include participation in PayPal guest checkout trials through the E2E-PLAORD-001 initiative, emphasizing its role in implementing contemporary e-commerce payment flows. The storefront's staging environment is accessible via stag-platypus-au.accentgra.com, and internally, the supporting API project is designated as pla-au. Overall, Platypus AU represents a technologically integrated and locally tailored e-commerce platform focused on delivering a seamless shopping experience for Platypus products within the Australian market.&lt;SEP&gt;A single representative storefront scope used by default for initial implementations of new slow or external payment flows.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific storefront limited to Platypus AU for the E2E-PLAORD-001 project, not including the other 7 storefronts.&lt;SEP&gt;A storefront brand on the AU staging environment, explicitly excluded from the storefront loop due to internal server errors from the createCustomer GraphQL mutation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-18c320b704b53c1b59c41f904f29e640-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf017a813cd0b782aef34bc894b9789d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a74540e7570b89ad3bb5cb22795ee605-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cecb0d91ce73637998acce9c5c61beac-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cecb0d91ce73637998acce9c5c61beac-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-89278d88eec2b6ee50a522529e8ddbde-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-161b36b883451ba6736c2ae4b3738bcc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ddca318d24811cc5b8909ad5fe282759-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a10959480a72a6acd62582bf626094f7-chunk-000</data>
