  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A logging or testing practice mentioned as part of feedback preferences, likely providing non-strict assertions.&lt;SEP&gt;SoftExpect is a drop-in replacement for the expect assertion with no logger integration, used in API tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A method for soft assertions in tests but does not log results internally.&lt;SEP&gt;A soft assertion method used to verify conditions without halting test execution upon failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Assertion method used in tests that does not log internally, distinct from softAssert fixture.</data>
