<node id="Skechers AU">
  <data key="d0">Skechers AU</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Skechers AU is the Australian ecommerce storefront for the Skechers brand, operating as a localized online platform tailored to the Australian market. It functions on the GRA storefront framework and employs the PageBuilder-Banner-root pattern, similar to its New Zealand counterpart, Skechers NZ. The site features key integrations such as TrueFit, an online fitting tool, and Afterpay, a popular buy-now-pay-later payment option, enhancing the shopping experience for Australian consumers.

This Australian Skechers storefront is part of multiple end-to-end localization and cart functionality tests, including E2E-LOC-001, E2E-LOC-004, and E2E-CART-003. During these evaluations, specific issues have been identified, such as silent add-to-cart failures that result in cart empties before the checkout step 10, concurrency problems within the cart overlay during testing, and occasional test skips when products lack purchasable sizes. These findings highlight challenges in maintaining seamless cart and checkout processes on the site.

Skechers AU operates on a Progressive Web App (PWA) Studio technology stack and includes user interface elements in the flyout menu such as "Track My Order," "Delivery," "Returns," "FAQs," and "Contact Us." Notably, despite extensive customer support options, there is no explicit "Help" link present in the flyout navigation. Additionally, the site participates in loyalty programs by enabling customers to earn Qantas Points on their purchases, further localizing the shopping experience for Australian users.

The ecommerce storefront's staging environment is accessible via the URL stag-skechers-au.accentgra.com and is supported by the API project identified as skx-au. Together, these components form a comprehensive Australian-focused online retail ecosystem for Skechers, emphasizing regional customization while sharing technological patterns with nearby markets.&lt;SEP&gt;An Australian storefront previously believed to have a shipping-address field-pattern mismatch.&lt;SEP&gt;A storefront brand where the test skipped due to genuine staging stock unavailability of "Go Walk" products across scanned products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-18c320b704b53c1b59c41f904f29e640-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf017a813cd0b782aef34bc894b9789d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf017a813cd0b782aef34bc894b9789d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a74540e7570b89ad3bb5cb22795ee605-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cecb0d91ce73637998acce9c5c61beac-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cecb0d91ce73637998acce9c5c61beac-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-89278d88eec2b6ee50a522529e8ddbde-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a10959480a72a6acd62582bf626094f7-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">ecommerce-storefronts.md&lt;SEP&gt;gra-storefront-tech-notes.md&lt;SEP&gt;ecommerce-smoke-spec-catalog.md&lt;SEP&gt;ecommerce-header-help-gotcha.md&lt;SEP&gt;ecommerce-pdp-page-gotchas.md&lt;SEP&gt;e2e-chkout-004-shipping-method.md&lt;SEP&gt;e2e-chkout-009-checkout-address-prefill.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785682490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Skechers AU</data>
</node>
<node id="Skechers NZ">
  <data key="d0">Skechers NZ</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Skechers NZ is an ecommerce storefront based in New Zealand that specializes in selling Skechers branded products. This online storefront operates with a staging URL at stag-skechers-nz.accentgra.com and is distinct in that it does not participate in earning Qantas Points. As the New Zealand division of Skechers, it incorporates localized features to tailor the shopping experience to the regional market.

The website is notable for its specific HTML structure, particularly on its homepage, which contains nine `&lt;h1&gt;` elements, eight of which are empty, while one includes text associated with a promotional banner. This structural detail differentiates Skechers NZ from other closely related storefronts, such as Skechers AU, despite sharing many common properties with them. The differences in HTML heading structure indicate targeted localization efforts.

Skechers NZ has been involved in end-to-end localization testing processes, specifically tests labeled E2E-LOC-002 and E2E-LOC-004, aimed at ensuring the site’s regional adaptation. However, it experiences technical challenges related to concurrency-sensitive race condition failures during cart overlay tests, revealing issues with simultaneous interactions on the site’s cart interface.

Further testing complexities arise from the Region/State combobox selector functionality. This selector remains unconfirmed or was not found during testing, leading to the skipping of tests that depend on this feature. This suggests a potential gap in the user interface or back-end handling of regional state selection within the storefront.

Overall, Skechers NZ is an ecommerce platform with regional customization and localized structural elements designed for New Zealand customers. Despite its close relationship to the Australian Skechers storefront, it maintains distinct properties and faces specific technical and functionality challenges related to localization and user interface components.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-18c320b704b53c1b59c41f904f29e640-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c9488069466f7da02e04d0a79614e167-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf017a813cd0b782aef34bc894b9789d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cecb0d91ce73637998acce9c5c61beac-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a10959480a72a6acd62582bf626094f7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a10959480a72a6acd62582bf626094f7-chunk-001</data>
